course: dictionary
lesson: 13582
title: A careful cut: incision
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An incision is a cut that is made on purpose, carefully and neatly, usually with a sharp tool. When you meet a new word, look at the words around it for clues. «The surgeon made a small incision in her arm, then closed it with stitches.» A surgeon is a doctor who operates, and stitches are used to sew a cut shut, so an incision must be a careful cut.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The gardener made a neat incision in the stem with a sharp knife.» If you swap in "a neat cut in the stem with a sharp knife", the sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Notice the phrases that often go with it: «make an incision», «a small incision», «a surgical incision». The word is a noun, so one cut is an incision and more than one cut is incisions. Remember that a neat, careful cut is what the word means, not a cut made by accident.
fact: An incision is a careful, neat cut made with a sharp tool.
fact: «Incision» is a noun. One is an incision, and more than one is incisions.
fact: A surgeon often makes an incision during an operation, and then closes it with stitches.
fact: Phrases to learn: «make an incision», «a small incision», «a surgical incision».
fact: Your front teeth are called incisors. The name comes from the same Latin word for cutting.
exercise: «The surgeon made a small incision so she could mend the bone.» What is an incision? | A loud noise | A soft pillow | *A careful cut | A kind of bird
exercise: «The nurse closed the incision with neat stitches.» What did the nurse do to the incision? | *Closed it with neat stitches | Ate it for lunch | Hid it in a drawer | Painted it blue
exercise: Which of these is an incision? | A soft blanket | *A neat cut made with a sharp tool | A big hug | A warm bath
test: «The gardener made a neat incision in the stem with a sharp knife.» What is an incision here? | *A neat cut | A sunny day | A tall plant | A pot of soil
test: Dad says, «Make a small incision, not a big one.» What does a small incision mean? | A loud shout | A big hole in the wall | A kind of sweet | *A little, careful cut
exam: Which phrase uses incision correctly? | *Make a small incision | Wear an incision | Sing an incision | Eat a sleepy incision
